00:01:22.494 --> 00:01:24.192
- There's four things when
someone gives you feedback,

00:01:24.192 --> 00:01:26.261
or criticism, however it's intended,

00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:27.608
whether ill or positive.

00:01:27.608 --> 00:01:30.493
And, so one is, not to take it
in, but to kind of catch it.

00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:31.560
I think of it like a catcher's mitt.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.318
If you tell me something,
you come across this way,

00:01:34.318 --> 00:01:36.545
I'll grab it, and then I'll
look at it and I'll think,

00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:37.712
"Okay, is it true?"

00:01:37.712 --> 00:01:38.701
If it's true, cool.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:40.256
I'll put it in and learn from it.

00:01:40.256 --> 00:01:42.136
If I think it's not true,
cool, I'll throw it away.

00:01:42.136 --> 00:01:42.995
No harm, no foul.

00:01:42.995 --> 00:01:44.605
I'm not going to dwell on it, right?

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.248
And I think everybody
needs this in this world,

00:01:46.248 --> 00:01:48.424
cause most of us are on social media,

00:01:48.424 --> 00:01:49.949
and we're all getting like,

00:01:49.949 --> 00:01:52.764
all our thoughts are getting
picked apart all the time.

00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:54.502
So we really need this more than ever.

00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:57.213
Then the third one, is, you
get it and it's a maybe.

00:01:57.213 --> 00:01:58.046
Well, I'm not sure.

00:01:58.046 --> 00:01:59.367
You said this about me, I'm not sure.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:00.464
You know, what do you guys think?

00:02:00.464 --> 00:02:01.297
You know, what do you think?

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:02.914
I'll ask my friends and
I'll ask other people

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:05.351
and get some feedback and if it's true,

00:02:05.351 --> 00:02:06.397
Cool, maybe I'll learn from it.

00:02:06.397 --> 00:02:07.230
If everyone's like,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.066
"This is total nonsense,
ignore that dude."

00:02:09.066 --> 00:02:10.313
I throw it out.

00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:11.527
But then there's a fourth one.

00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:13.023
And this is where the real growth is.

00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:13.949
Do you know what the fourth one is?

00:02:13.949 --> 00:02:14.782
- I don't.

00:02:14.782 --> 00:02:18.477
- The fourth one is, you
get it, you throw it out.

00:02:18.477 --> 00:02:21.680
I'm talking to you and then
maybe later I'm talking to you,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.891
I get it, and I'm like,

00:02:22.891 --> 00:02:23.797
"No, it's not true."

00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:25.707
I throw it out, and then later
