Say, "Well, I didn't cause it."

00:09:26.766 --> 00:09:28.165
You just say simply,

00:09:28.165 --> 00:09:32.279
"Ah, they're in a bad
place. I hope they're okay."

00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:35.025
I think it's a real, true personal power

00:09:35.025 --> 00:09:36.975
to be able to walk by negative people,

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.150
and still say,

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:42.608
"I wish you nothing but
joy and health and strength

00:09:42.608 --> 00:09:44.626
"and love in your life."

00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:46.711
To have that hope for people,

00:09:46.711 --> 00:09:50.687
even when they're in a bad
place, that's humanity.

00:09:50.687 --> 00:09:53.020
- Your critics don't matter.

00:09:55.722 --> 00:09:59.639
Has there ever been a
statue built of a critic?

00:10:00.831 --> 00:10:04.912
I remember the great writer
Paulo Coelho said that

00:10:04.912 --> 00:10:09.527
he doesn't think about his
critics, that's their job.

00:10:09.527 --> 00:10:12.880
And it made me realize
that, that is so true.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.225
You see so many of us.

00:10:15.225 --> 00:10:19.392
We spend our time worrying
about people who don't serve us.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:26.157
I say, I am letting go of
whatever no longer serves me

00:10:27.497 --> 00:10:31.458
to make space for what
the hell inspires me.

00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:32.791
And that is that

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.737
beautiful pirana baby, right?

00:10:37.953 --> 00:10:41.703
Now, in the grand scheme
of criticism, right?

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.843
We can write essays.

00:10:45.843 --> 00:10:50.763
We can write essays on criticism,
because it's so exciting.

00:10:50.763 --> 00:10:52.704
Look at it like this,

00:10:52.704 --> 00:10:55.037
many people stop having fun,

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:01.150
you play it safe when
someone criticises you.

00:11:02.224 --> 00:11:04.703
So when I first started to
make videos, someone said,

00:11:04.703 --> 00:11:08.608
"Gosh, Ralph, that video was so long."

00:11:08.608 --> 00:11:10.641
It was only four minutes.

00:11:10.641 --> 00:11:11.474
So I said,

00:11:11.474 --> 00:11:12.807
"Actually, okay.

00:11:14.259 --> 00:11:16.034
"I'm going to take on board what you say."

00:11:16.034 --> 00:11:20.201
And the next video, the
next video was 26 minutes.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.800
Can I get a hello there?

00:11:25.551 --> 00:11:27.188
You see?

00:11:27.188 --> 00:11:31.259
I made videos with my
hair all over the place.

00:11:31.259 --> 00:11:35.426
And some people said, "Ralph,
your hair looks terrible."

00:11:37.569 --> 00:11:40.291
Do you know how I felt?

00:11:40.291 --> 00:11:42.076
Yeah, I felt like that.

00:11:42.076 --> 00:11:43.703
It was really hard.

00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:45.340
And, I thought,

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.828
"Okay, I've got to make my hair like this,

00:11:46.828 --> 00:11:48.621
"I've got to make my hair like that."

00:11:48.621 --> 00:11:52.788
Then I said, "Actually, my
hair does not define who I am.

00:11:53.706 --> 00:11:55.180
"I am not my hair.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.364
"I am so much more."

00:11:57.364 --> 00:12:00.765
So that gave me the
strength to say, "Screw it."

00:12:00.765 --> 00:12:02.284
And for many years,

00:12:02.284 --> 00:12:03.214
I made videos

00:12:03.214 --> 00:12:05.961
with my hair all over
the place and guess what?

00:12:05.961 --> 00:12:06.794
I loved it.

00:12:06.794 --> 00:12:08.794
Can I get a hello there?

00:12:10.465 --> 00:12:11.818
Do whatever you want.

00:12:11.818 --> 00:12:13.322
Say whatever you want.

00:12:13.322 --> 00:12:14.953
Go wherever you want.

00:12:14.953 --> 00:12:19.120
And if anybody's got a
problem with that, screw them.

00:12:21.603 --> 00:12:23.091
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:23.091 --> 00:12:25.779
I made this video because
one of my teammates, Ivan,

00:12:25.779 --> 00:12:27.635
who does a lot of the
research for these videos,

00:12:27.635 --> 00:12:29.088
wanted to put this one together.

00:12:29.088 --> 00:12:30.985
So, thank you, Ivan, for all the work.

00:12:30.985 --> 00:12:32.603
And if there's a topic
that you'd like us to cover

00:12:32.603 --> 00:12:34.986
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:12:34.986 --> 00:12:36.517
please leave it in the comments below

00:12:36.517 --> 00:12:37.683
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:37.683 --> 00:12:38.672
I'm also curious to figure out

00:12:38.672 --> 00:12:41.074
what was the biggest lesson
that you took from this?

00:12:41.074 --> 00:12:43.443
How are you having a hard
time dealing with haters?

00:12:43.443 --> 00:12:44.318
And maybe,

00:12:44.318 --> 00:12:47.147
did one of these strategies
stand out from the rest?

00:12:47.147 --> 00:12:48.718
I'm super curious to figure it out.

00:12:48.718 --> 00:12:51.025
Leave it in the comments,
your experiences below,

00:12:51.025 --> 00:12:52.737
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:52.737 --> 00:12:55.086
Finally, I want to give a
shout-out to my publisher,

00:12:55.086 --> 00:12:56.255
Marian Lizzi.

00:12:56.255 --> 00:12:57.259
Thank you so much, Marian,

00:12:57.259 --> 00:12:59.547
for all your support in
the launch of my book

00:12:59.547 --> 00:13:00.637
Your One Word,

00:13:00.637 --> 00:13:03.922
and for posting that awesome
unboxing picture on Instagram.

00:13:03.922 --> 00:13:05.838
I really, really, really,
really appreciate it.

00:13:05.838 --> 00:13:07.092
So thank you guys, again for watching.

00:13:07.092 --> 00:13:08.451
I believe in you.

00:13:08.451 --> 00:13:10.530
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.474
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:12.474 --> 00:13:14.019
Much love.

00:13:14.019 --> 00:13:15.519
I'll see you soon.

00:13:21.252 --> 00:13:24.514
- I'm one who always welcomes criticism.

00:13:24.514 --> 00:13:27.939
And I encourage people, you
should should welcome criticism,

00:13:27.939 --> 00:13:31.194
and be bold enough to give criticism.

00:13:31.194 --> 00:13:35.003
If the criticism is
coming out of benevolence,

00:13:35.003 --> 00:13:39.170
that someone is criticising
so that I can become better,

00:13:41.139 --> 00:13:42.612
then it is always welcome.

00:13:42.612 --> 00:13:45.882
But if someone is criticising
just out of jealousy

00:13:45.882 --> 00:13:50.596
or trying to pull someone
down, then that is not good.

00:13:50.596 --> 00:13:54.179
Then that is coming
from a malefic mindset.

00:13:57.287 --> 00:14:02.019
So, constructive criticism, I
feel everyone should welcome.

00:14:02.019 --> 00:14:03.765
Criticism with compassion.

00:14:03.765 --> 00:14:05.348
Criticism with love

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:08.745
is most adorable thing.

00:14:08.745 --> 00:14:10.628
And it should always be welcomed.

00:14:10.628 --> 00:14:12.402
- Use their energy.

00:14:12.402 --> 00:14:15.139
Use that energy they put out there.

00:14:15.139 --> 00:14:19.306
Use that challenge for your
own character development.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.133
Really.

00:14:21.133 --> 00:14:21.966
See?

00:14:21.966 --> 00:14:23.197
When somebody's negative around me,

00:14:23.197 --> 00:14:24.969
I don't sit there and I
don't become a victim.

00:14:24.969 --> 00:14:26.873
Oh gosh, they're such negative...

00:14:26.873 --> 00:14:29.717
I don't go home and assume their energy,

00:14:29.717 --> 00:14:30.965
and now I'm negative.

00:14:30.965 --> 00:14:31.798
Instead, I go,

00:14:31.798 --> 00:14:32.631
"You know what?

00:14:32.631 --> 00:14:33.932
"This is a moment to test.

00:14:33.932 --> 00:14:37.932
"Am I really in command of
my emotions and how I think?

00:14:37.932 --> 00:14:39.099
"Or are they?"

00:14:39.099 --> 00:14:41.450
Am I giving my power over to the world,

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:43.592
so that they can just take my energy

00:14:43.592 --> 00:14:47.101
and turn it to what they
want or am I in charge?

00:14:47.101 --> 00:14:49.795
So I use it as a challenge.

00:14:49.795 --> 00:14:51.667
Not as something, I
don't have to challenge

00:14:51.667 --> 00:14:53.304
or change them immediately.

00:14:53.304 --> 00:14:54.929
I'll get to that point.

00:14:54.929 --> 00:14:55.978
But I get to the point where I say,

00:14:55.978 --> 00:14:56.954
"You know what?

00:14:56.954 --> 00:14:58.620
"Huh, here's a little
challenge the world's

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.672
"throwing me right now.

00:14:59.672 --> 00:15:00.836
"Can I stay on my game?

00:15:00.836 --> 00:15:02.354
"Can I stay centered?

00:15:02.354 --> 00:15:03.873
"Can I stay peaceful?

00:15:03.873 --> 00:15:05.226
"Can I stay calm?

00:15:05.226 --> 00:15:08.577
"Can I stay present, right here, right now

00:15:08.577 --> 00:15:10.881
"and not have to run away from it.

00:15:10.881 --> 00:15:15.049
"Not have to pretend it's
not there, but use it."

00:15:15.049 --> 00:15:16.744
And I encourage you to do that.

00:15:16.744 --> 00:15:18.026
Because, if it's just something that you

00:15:18.026 --> 00:15:19.290
immediately complain about,

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:23.402
well then, in your complaint
you've just let them win.

00:15:23.402 --> 00:15:26.009
Their negativity has turned you into

00:15:26.009 --> 00:15:28.714
noticing what is negative and you lost.

00:15:28.714 --> 00:15:29.562
You're not winning.

00:15:29.562 --> 00:15:32.609
Even if you can critically
throw a barb at it,

00:15:32.609 --> 00:15:35.425
make fun of it, you're still losing.

00:15:35.425 --> 00:15:38.170
You're being sucked into
their pools of pessimism.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.911
You're drowning.

00:15:39.911 --> 00:15:41.546
So I say, use it.

00:15:41.546 --> 00:15:43.835
Recognize it and use it.

00:15:43.835 --> 00:15:45.345
- Harshest criticism.

00:15:45.345 --> 00:15:48.582
Look, the thing is, you
know, in the beginning,

00:15:48.582 --> 00:15:50.338
it's a little funky but you got to realize

00:15:50.338 --> 00:15:52.971
that everybody nowadays has an opinion.

00:15:52.971 --> 00:15:54.738
Everybody's a critic.

00:15:54.738 --> 00:15:55.618
And, you know,

00:15:55.618 --> 00:15:58.581
you can watch my video on
YouTube and leave a comment.

00:15:58.581 --> 00:16:03.080
You can go to iTunes and buy
my album and leave a comment.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.722
You can Tweet, whatever, you know.

00:16:04.722 --> 00:16:06.922
And, you're going to drive yourself crazy

00:16:06.922 --> 00:16:10.422
if you really take those things seriously.

00:16:12.287 --> 00:16:14.096
Just, not everyone's going to love you.

